    "description": "D7 review item P2: review question"
  },
  "reviewP2Why": "Ibn 'Abd al-Barr is a foundational Maliki authority; his chapter would corroborate or refine the matn positions, particularly on isfar and the shared windows.",
  "@reviewP2Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item P2: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewP2Evidence": "Edition verified, text unread — ed. Dr. Muhammad Ahid Ould Maddik al-Mauritani, Maktabat al-Riyad al-Haditha, 1978.",
  "@reviewP2Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item P2: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewP3Question": "Read the continuation pages of al-Hattab's Mawahib al-Jalil muwaqit chapter on islamweb covering 'isha/shafaq and fajr/subh.",
  "@reviewP3Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item P3: review question"
  },
  "reviewP3Why": "The Mawahib is the school's great commentary on Khalil; these sections likely contain the most detailed classical discussion of the two twilight boundaries the app must approximate.",
  "@reviewP3Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item P3: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewP3Evidence": "Partially read — the 'isha/fajr continuation pages exist on islamweb but their URLs were not located without guessing.",
  "@reviewP3Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item P3: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewP4Question": "Collate the matn wording at the daruri passage — «واثم الا لعذر» is confirmed as matn; the possible «وعلى جماعة آخره» variant needs checking against Dardir/Dasuqi.",
  "@reviewP4Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item P4: review question"
  },
  "reviewP4Why": "The daruri-sin wording appears in the app's two-tier display; the matn must be quoted exactly.",
  "@reviewP4Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item P4: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewP4Evidence": "Unresolved textual variant.",
  "@reviewP4Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item P4: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewP5Question": "Obtain the Mauritanian ministry's calculation methodology — angles, method name, asr convention, ihtiyat — from an official source.",
  "@reviewP5Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item P5: review question"
  },
  "reviewP5Why": "Closes the inference gap behind the Mauritanian Scholarly Profile investigation.",
  "@reviewP5Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item P5: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewP5Evidence": "Unpublished; MWL 18/17 + ~1–2 min is inference only.",
  "@reviewP5Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item P5: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewP6Question": "Determine whether Bin Bayyah, Ould Dedew, or Ould 'Adud has a recorded position on prayer-time calculation conventions (angles, methods) — distinct from their general fiqh teachings.",
  "@reviewP6Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item P6: review question"
  },
  "reviewP6Why": "A recorded position would anchor the Mauritanian profile; continued silence must be recorded as a negative finding, not filled.",
  "@reviewP6Why": {
    "description": "D7 review item P6: why-it-matters"
  },
  "reviewP6Evidence": "No web evidence found — may exist in offline Arabic print or lessons.",
  "@reviewP6Evidence": {
    "description": "D7 review item P6: evidence status"
  },
  "reviewP7Question": "Identify the scholar al-Hattab cites for latitude-specific prayer-time tables («أبو مقرع») in the Mawahib passage.",
  "@reviewP7Question": {
    "description": "D7 review item P7: review question"
  },
  "reviewP7Why": "Historical completeness of the miqat record; does not affect any app parameter.",
  "@reviewP7Why": {
